+applied. `authority-repair.patch` records the changes against that exact input.
+`SHA256SUMS.json` identifies the delivered files. The earlier review is retained
+in `FINDINGS.md`, clearly marked as historical; its original green totals are not
+the results of this run. No unseen Claude implementation has been merged.
+
+Here “R2” and “R3” mean the `invariant_guard.py` findings in the original
+`FINDINGS.md`, not the separately numbered audience-release findings.
+
+## What the newer upload changes
+
+There are **10 changed files** between the September 12 and September 13 uploads:
+four Marshmallow Python files, `FINDINGS.md`, and five saved runtime/log files.
+All **152 files under `driftcore/` are identical** between those inputs, including
+the guard, coordinator, identity verifier and broker. This newer upload does not
+contain the unfinished authority redesign quoted from Claude.
+
+The 19 previously reviewed authorization repair files apply without source
+conflicts. This merge preserves the newer `marshmallow/analyze.py`,
+`marshmallow/marshmallow.py`, `marshmallow/runner.py` and `marshmallow/selftest.py`
+byte-for-byte. Their self-test now reports **43/43**, covering the added missing-data,
+shutdown, logging-effect and protocol checks. The Marshmallow README now tells
+reviewers to require a successful self-test instead of its stale 30/30 literal.
+No live model or external API was called.
+
+The original September 13 saved runtime files are preserved in the package.
+Runtime changes generated by verification were confined to disposable test copies.
+The delivered repair artifact is updated to this base; use its current contents
